1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,217
My engineer, three rooms, and a hulk nobody has opened in years.

2
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:15,233
She is the same person on the bridge and aboard it, and all of it is text I wrote in one file.

3
00:00:15,683 --> 00:00:17,857
Today you write your own.

4
00:00:19,057 --> 00:00:21,665
A new section at the bottom.

5
00:00:22,115 --> 00:00:28,202
The word crew on the first line of the fence says what it is.

6
00:00:28,652 --> 00:00:30,391
Ship says whose crew.

7
00:00:30,841 --> 00:00:39,537
And Names: locked says these are my people: without it, a player who has saved their own name keeps it.

8
00:00:39,987 --> 00:00:46,509
Then one record per person: the console they sit at, a face, and a job.

9
00:00:46,959 --> 00:00:52,176
Whoever sits at Engineering is the Chief, here and aboard the hulk.

10
00:00:53,376 --> 00:00:55,550
A room is a record.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,522
One line starting with a percent sign: what the party finds when they walk in.

12
00:01:02,972 --> 00:01:04,711
Then the ways out.

13
00:01:05,161 --> 00:01:09,074
Words in square brackets are what the crew reads.

14
00:01:09,524 --> 00:01:14,307
The key in round brackets is the room it leads to.

15
00:01:14,757 --> 00:01:21,278
And empty round brackets lead nowhere: that choice ends the visit and sends everyone home.

16
00:01:22,478 --> 00:01:28,130
Two rules, and they are the difference between a place and a trap.

17
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:31,189
Every room has a way back.

18
00:01:31,639 --> 00:01:34,248
Every room has a way home.

19
00:01:34,698 --> 00:01:49,915
Check them by eye, because lint only helps with half of it: it warns if a choice points at a room that does not exist, and says nothing about a room with no way out.

20
00:01:51,115 --> 00:01:53,289
Something has to say when.

21
00:01:53,739 --> 00:01:58,087
Our quest already knows the moment: the ship is alongside.

22
00:01:58,537 --> 00:02:05,059
So the quest sends a signal when it completes, and this card listens for it.

23
00:02:05,509 --> 00:02:08,987
You paste it; you do not write it.

24
00:02:09,437 --> 00:02:11,611
One line reads the rooms.

25
00:02:12,061 --> 00:02:23,365
And one line runs the whole visit: it opens the party, starts the first room, and when the last choice is taken it brings everyone home.

26
00:02:23,815 --> 00:02:33,815
Three things on the card are yours to change: the signal name, the name of the place, and the room they arrive in.

27
00:02:35,015 --> 00:02:36,015
Lint. Clean.

28
00:02:36,465 --> 00:02:40,378
And here is the one mistake it does catch.

29
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:44,622
Engineering, and I am Chief Okoro. Alongside.

30
00:02:45,072 --> 00:02:51,159
The quest completes, and the party forms. Down. The airlock. Aft. Back. Forward. Back.

31
00:02:51,609 --> 00:02:56,391
And home: I did not press anything to get back here.

32
00:02:57,591 --> 00:03:01,939
Add a fourth room, and a third person for Helm.

33
00:03:02,389 --> 00:03:08,041
Give the room a way in, a way back and a way home.

34
00:03:08,491 --> 00:03:11,535
Next time, everyone gets their own menu.
